{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-39478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral of the form \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{c}^{d}{\\int }_{e}^{f}…\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given the limits for $x,y,$ and $z,$ we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-39478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2y)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nGiven that the triple integral above is considered over the rectangular box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a+b=1+4=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 5}\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral of the form \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{c}^{d}{\\int }_{e}^{f}…\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given the limits for $x,y,$ and $z,$ we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+xy+{z}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz\n$$\n\nGiven that the triple integral above is considered over the rectangular box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le e,\\,1\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{e}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a+b=-2+3=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+1"] ["math" "e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2\\sqrt{3},\\,2\\le y\\le 3,\\,-3\\le z\\le -2}\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral of the form \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{c}^{d}{\\int }_{e}^{f}…\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given the limits for $x,y,$ and $z,$ we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}{\\int }_{1}^{2\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-39541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}{\\int }_{1}^{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}{\\int }_{1}^{2\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39541" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}{\\int }_{1}^{2\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y{x}^{3}({z}^{2}-1)}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}]\\times [0,1]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{y{e}^{z}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot y\\cdot {e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & ={[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{\\sqrt{2}/4}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [{e}^{z}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{2}+2\\sqrt{2})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0)\\cdot (5-1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}(z-1)}{x}\\,\\text{d}V,\\,\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,1\\le z\\le 3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}(z-1)}{x}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{y}^{2}(z-1)}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[1,e]\\times [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{y}^{2}(z-1)}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot {y}^{2}\\cdot (z-1)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{3}(z-1)\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{3}(z-1)\\,\\text{d}z & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}-z]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (\\frac{8}{3}-0)\\cdot (\\frac{9}{2}-3-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161362" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161362" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161362" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{16}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}V,\\,\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,0\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[1,e]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z+y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{e}^{z}\\cdot {e}^{y}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & ={[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}_{1}^{e}\\cdot {[{e}^{y}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot {[{e}^{z}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (3-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-39475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-39475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V,\\,\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le z\\le 1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]\\times [\\frac{1}{2},1]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [\\operatorname{sin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{1}{z}]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =(1+1)\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot (-1+2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{z}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,1\\le z\\le e}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{z}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R=[0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]\\times [-1,1]\\times [1,e]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =[{e}^{x}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot [y]_{-1}^{1}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡z]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(3-1)\\cdot (1-(-1))\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161277" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161277" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}z{e}^{x}+2y\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z{e}^{x}+2xy]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}z({e}^{3}-1)+2(3-0)y\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{3}-1)z+6y\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{3}-1)z+6y\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{3}-1)z+6y\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}\\,{z}^{2}+6yz]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}(1-0)+6y(1-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}+6y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}+6y\\,dy & ={[\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}\\,y+3{y}^{2}]}_{y=-1}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{2}(1-(-1))+3(1-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161368" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161368" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{e}^{3}"] ["math" "3({e}^{2}-2e)"] ["math" "3{e}^{2}+2"] ["math" "3{e}^{3}+1"] ["math" "{e}^{3}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161368" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{3}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $y,$ and then $z,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $y,$ and then $z,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dx]dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+xz]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}(1-0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(1-0)z\\,dy\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dy\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+z\\,dy]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+yz]}_{y=0}^{y=\\pi }\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}(0-0)+(\\pi -0)z\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\pi z\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\pi z\\,dz & =\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}z\\,dz \\\\  & =\\pi {[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3-2\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi -2}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "] ["math" "\\pi -1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\le z\\le 2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{2}(x-y){e}^{z}\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x-y){e}^{z}]_{z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{z=2}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)({e}^{2}-2)\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[({e}^{2}-2){\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-y)\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2){[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-xy]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)[\\frac{1}{2}(1-0)-(1-0)y]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-y)dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2}-2)(\\frac{1}{2}-y)dy & =({e}^{2}-2){\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2}-y\\,dy \\\\  & =({e}^{2}-2){[\\frac{1}{2}y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=-1}^{y=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-2}{2}(0-(-1)+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2({e}^{2}-3)"] ["math" "2{e}^{2}"] ["math" "2{e}^{2}-1"] ["math" "4{e}^{2}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161374" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2}-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}5x-3y\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-1\\le z\\le 0}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}5x-3y\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}5x-3y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}5x-3y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}5x-3y\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[5xy-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}5x(2-0)-\\frac{3}{2}(4-0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}10x-6\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}10x-6\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-1}^{0}10x-6\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(10x-6)z]_{z=-1}^{z=0}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(10x-6)(0-(-1))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10x-6\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}10x-6\\,dx & =[5{x}^{2}-6x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =5(1-0)-6(1-0) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{10}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,dV\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\text{d}V=\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }z\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{y}^{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+x{y}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi }\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}-z(-1-1)+{y}^{2}(\\pi -0)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2z+\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2z+\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2z+\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{z}^{2}+\\pi {y}^{2}z]_{z=-1}^{z=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-1)+\\pi {y}^{2}(2-(-1))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3+3\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3+3\\pi {y}^{2}\\,dy & =[3y+\\pi {y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =3(1-0)+\\pi (1-0) \\\\  & =3+\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e99f490ef0a34e50681a3eb8b2402752462ed7c81f12f29d40f2fb723072030b"} {"question" "q-161367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2-3\\pi "] ["math" "2\\pi -3"] ["math" "3+\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "q-161367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/state.json" "file_sha256" "8d31831d3e177ef375c078a0077e2d365bd078d51bded422b408f5d6aaa00ea0"} {"question" "e-11585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\iiint\\limits_{R} (x+y+z)^2 \\: \\textrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box\n\n$$\nR = \\bigg\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0\\leq z \\leq 2 \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral of the form \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\int_a^b  \\int_c^d  \\int_e^f \\ldots \\: \\textrm{d}y\\:  \\textrm{d}z\\:  \\textrm{d}x .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/example-11585.json" "file_sha256" "b06b4e4c3667a8e795cb597f867e63dfd6e88f3ec053fef11e7258c69ef8f3b8"} {"question" "e-11585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given the limits for $x,y,$ and $z,$ we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(x+y+z)^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+y+z)^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/example-11585.json" "file_sha256" "b06b4e4c3667a8e795cb597f867e63dfd6e88f3ec053fef11e7258c69ef8f3b8"} {"question" "e-7263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \n\\iiint\\limits_{R} y \\cos{x} \\sin{z} \\: \\textrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the box $R = \\bigg\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\pi \\bigg\\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/example-7263.json" "file_sha256" "9cab32210d03f300d93a13703bbc0a574d191e73b7bc7b17c4a2c2e1a6d7e3c0"} {"question" "e-7263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration $R = \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right]\\times[0,1]\\times\\left[0,\\pi\\right]$ is a rectangular box, and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z & =[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z]_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0)\\cdot (1-(-1)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/example-7263.json" "file_sha256" "9cab32210d03f300d93a13703bbc0a574d191e73b7bc7b17c4a2c2e1a6d7e3c0"} {"question" "e-12391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "By integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R z-xy  \\: \\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nover the rectangular box $R = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\:0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 1 \\leq z \\leq 3 \\right\\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/example-12391.json" "file_sha256" "c902767ad58c18e82d88acbe880e18b5fcb7220e10255c769354d2a5f7f6bb2a"} {"question" "e-12391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} z-xy \\: \\textrm{d}V\n= \n\\int_{-1}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{1}^{3} z-xy \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z,$ then $x,$ and then $y,$ we write $\\textrm d V = \\textrm d z\\:\\textrm d x\\:\\textrm d y.$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}z-xy\\,dz\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}z-xy\\,dz]dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}-xyz]}_{z=1}^{z=3}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(9-1)-xy(3-1)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-2xy\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-2xy\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-2yx\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[4x-y{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}4(2-0)-y({2}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}8-4y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}8-4y\\,dy & =[8y-2{y}^{2}]_{y=-1}^{y=1} \\\\  & =8(1-(-1))-2({1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2-2(1-1) \\\\  & =16-0 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060551/example-12391.json" "file_sha256" "c902767ad58c18e82d88acbe880e18b5fcb7220e10255c769354d2a5f7f6bb2a"}] "usage" {"e-12391" [] "q-39475" [] "e-11585" [] "e-7263" [] "q-161374" []} "basis" 1942 "retractions" [[17592186129675 :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)\\frac{e^{z + y}}{x}dV$,\nover the box $R = {(x, y, z): 1 \\le x \\le e, 0 \\le y \\le \\ln 3, 0 \\le z \\le \\ln 2}$."] [17592186129450 :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)(x - y)e^{z}dV$\nover the rectangular box $R = {(x, y, z): 0 \\le x \\le 1,-1 \\le y \\le 0, \\ln 2 \\le z \\le 2}$."] [17592186128784 :question/problem "Express the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_{R} (x+y+z)^2 \\: \\textrm{d}V$\nover the box\n$R = \\bigg\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0\\leq z \\leq 2 \\bigg\\}$\nas a repeated integral of the form\n$\\displaystyle \\int_a^b \\int_c^d \\int_e^f \\ldots \\: \\textrm{d}y\\: \\textrm{d}z\\: \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186128784 :question/worked-solution "Given the limits for $x,y$, and $z$, we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∭_(R)(x + y + z)^{2}dV &= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}(x + y + z)^{2}dydzdx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128949 :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_{R} y \\cos{x} \\sin{z} \\: \\textrm{d}V$\nover the box $R = \\bigg\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\pi \\bigg\\}$."] [17592186128949 :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∭_(R)y\\cos x\\sin zdV &= ∫_{0}^{π}∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{π/2}y\\cos x\\sin zdxdydz\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration\n\n$$\nR = \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right]\\times[0,1]\\times\\left[0,\\pi\\right]\n$$\n\nis a rectangular box, and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z)$, we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n∫_{0}^{π/2}\\cos xdx∫_{0}^{1}ydy∫_{0}^{π}\\sin zdz\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{π/2}\\cos xdx∫_{0}^{1}ydy∫_{0}^{π}\\sin zdz &= [\\sin x]_{0}^{π/2} \\cdot [\\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{1} \\cdot [- \\cos z]_{0}^{π} \\\\\n&= (1 - 0) \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2} - 0) \\cdot (1 - (-1)) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128789 :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, evaluate the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R z-xy \\: \\mathrm{d}V$\nover the rectangular box $R = \\left\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\:0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 1 \\leq z \\leq 3 \\right\\}$."] [17592186128789 :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} z-xy \\: \\textrm{d}V = \\int_{-1}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{1}^{3} z-xy \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, we write\n\n$$\n\\textrm d V = \\textrm d z\\:\\textrm d x\\:\\textrm d y\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}∫_{1}^{3}z - xydzdxdy &= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}[∫_{1}^{3}z - xydz]dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}[\\frac{1}{2}z^{2} - xyz]_{z = 1}^{z = 3}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(9 - 1) - xy(3 - 1)dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}4 - 2xydxdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}4 - 2xydxdy &= ∫_{-1}^{1}[∫_{0}^{2}4 - 2yxdx]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}[4x - yx^{2}]_{x = 0}^{x = 2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}4(2 - 0) - y(2^{2} - 0)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}8 - 4ydy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{1}8 - 4ydy &= [8y - 2y^{2}]_{y =-1}^{y = 1} \\\\\n&= 8(1 - (-1)) - 2(1^{2} - (-1)^{2}) \\\\\n&= 8 \\cdot 2 - 2(1 - 1) \\\\\n&= 16 - 0 \\\\\n&= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186126507 17592186126508 17592186126509 17592186126510 17592186126511 17592186127845 17592186127846 17592186127847 17592186127848 17592186127849] "immutable_fields" [[17592186126506 :answer-field/correct] [17592186126506 :